      "message": "The zephyr test team can provide guidance and reviews for writing unit tests on new features like this one: zephyr-test-eng@google.com\n\nFor features that require setting a Kconfig option, I usually create a new test under `zephyr/test/drivers/`.  That way, you can set up your new Kconfig and add a basic test to validate that it works (in this case, validate that we turn the body detection on after we cycle up to S0, and off after we emulate a power down)",
